{"source": "/home/ubuntu/shiva-study-set/Shiva Sutras 3.32.mp3", "engine": "faster-whisper-base", "segments": [{"t": 0.08, "end": 4.08, "text": "Nanu-Evam-Srechti-Sethi-Laya-Vastrasu,"}, {"t": 4.08, "end": 10.08, "text": "Onyoni-Beda-Awasma-Ishu, Asya-Sorup-Anyatatam-Aya-Tam,"}, {"t": 10.08, "end": 15.58, "text": "It-Ashenga-Shantartha-Maha."}, {"t": 15.58, "end": 22.58, "text": "So, as he said in previous sutras, that this whole universe"}, {"t": 22.58, "end": 26.58, "text": "is expansion of his own glory,"}, {"t": 26.58, "end": 31.58, "text": "not only in creation but in protection and in destruction also."}, {"t": 32.58, "end": 36.58, "text": "In Srechti, in Sethi and in Samhara."}, {"t": 36.58, "end": 39.58, "text": "Now he argues, he puts question,"}, {"t": 39.58, "end": 42.58, "text": "Nanu-Evam-Srechti-Sethi-Laya-Vastrasu,"}, {"t": 42.58, "end": 46.58, "text": "in this way if Yogi feels that this whole universe"}, {"t": 46.58, "end": 49.58, "text": "is the expansion of his own nature,"}, {"t": 49.58, "end": 56.58, "text": "in creation, in protection and in destruction."}, {"t": 56.58, "end": 62.37, "text": "But his nature would be unchangeable then."}, {"t": 62.37, "end": 65.62, "text": "It will get its change."}, {"t": 65.62, "end": 70.62, "text": "In creation, it will have one way of being"}, {"t": 70.62, "end": 73.62, "text": "in protection another way,"}, {"t": 73.62, "end": 75.62, "text": "and in destruction another way."}, {"t": 75.62, "end": 78.62, "text": "So, his Surupa, his state of self"}, {"t": 78.62, "end": 83.28, "text": "won't remain unchangeable."}, {"t": 83.28, "end": 86.28, "text": "Asya-Sorup-Anyatatam-Aya-Tam,"}, {"t": 86.28, "end": 92.28, "text": "his original state of being"}, {"t": 92.28, "end": 96.28, "text": "will get changed every now and then."}, {"t": 96.28, "end": 101.85, "text": "For that, he puts the answer."}, {"t": 101.85, "end": 105.85, "text": "Tatt pravratava-pi-anirasa-sandhi-tribava-vat."}, {"t": 105.85, "end": 108.85, "text": "Tatt pravratava-pi,"}, {"t": 108.85, "end": 112.85, "text": "although he is bent upon creating the universe,"}, {"t": 112.85, "end": 116.85, "text": "protecting it and destroying it."}, {"t": 116.85, "end": 122.32, "text": "Even then, samvatribava-vat-anirasa,"}, {"t": 123.32, "end": 127.32, "text": "he does not get away from the being of his"}, {"t": 127.32, "end": 134.65, "text": "no worship, samvatribava-vat."}, {"t": 134.65, "end": 136.65, "text": "Just stop it."}, {"t": 136.65, "end": 139.65, "text": "Pravratava-pi-anirasa-sandhi-tribava-vat,"}, {"t": 139.65, "end": 142.65, "text": "although he is bent upon creating the universe,"}, {"t": 142.65, "end": 145.65, "text": "protecting it and destroying it."}, {"t": 145.65, "end": 152.65, "text": "But he does not get himself away from samvatribava."}, {"t": 152.65, "end": 157.65, "text": "Samvatribava means the state of subjectivity,"}, {"t": 157.65, "end": 160.65, "text": "the state of reality of self."}, {"t": 160.65, "end": 166.63, "text": "The reality of self remains same in creation,"}, {"t": 166.63, "end": 169.63, "text": "in protection and in destruction."}, {"t": 169.63, "end": 172.63, "text": "Teśāṁ śrīṣṭhādīnāṁ pravratava-pi,"}, {"t": 172.63, "end": 179.26, "text": "although he creates, he protects, and he destroys."}, {"t": 179.26, "end": 183.26, "text": "No, as he yoginā samvatribava-vat."}, {"t": 183.26, "end": 186.26, "text": "But this yogi is never,"}, {"t": 186.26, "end": 190.26, "text": "never becomes away from the samvatribava,"}, {"t": 190.26, "end": 193.26, "text": "the state of no worship."}, {"t": 193.26, "end": 196.26, "text": "That is the state where you get the āmātkāra,"}, {"t": 196.26, "end": 199.26, "text": "the bliss of tūrī, anākya."}, {"t": 199.26, "end": 202.26, "text": "Tūrī āmātkāra, maka-vimarsimayāt,"}, {"t": 202.26, "end": 207.26, "text": "upalabdṛta, and that is the real state of being no where."}, {"t": 207.26, "end": 209.26, "text": "Subjectivity."}, {"t": 209.26, "end": 212.26, "text": "And he is never nirasa-shchalanam."}, {"t": 212.26, "end": 215.26, "text": "He is never becomes away from that."}, {"t": 215.26, "end": 220.26, "text": "He is always with that in these three-fold actions."}, {"t": 220.26, "end": 222.26, "text": "Sreste, sreste and samhāra."}, {"t": 222.26, "end": 225.26, "text": "Tāt nirasa-shchalanam."}, {"t": 225.26, "end": 232.26, "text": "If he would remain away from that reality of self in these actions,"}, {"t": 232.26, "end": 235.26, "text": "kāśichatapi aprakāśanāt,"}, {"t": 235.26, "end": 239.26, "text": "the state of creation, the state of protection,"}, {"t": 239.26, "end": 241.26, "text": "and the state of destruction,"}, {"t": 241.26, "end": 243.26, "text": "wouldn't exist."}, {"t": 243.26, "end": 248.26, "text": "The existence comes from the power of no worship."}, {"t": 248.26, "end": 251.26, "text": "It is said, tātraivā."}, {"t": 251.26, "end": 258.15, "text": "Tātraivā means kālikā-kram, kālikram-kramśāstra."}, {"t": 258.15, "end": 263.15, "text": "Naśe, vidyā-prapaṁ teśya, sovāvo nāvineśete,"}, {"t": 263.15, "end": 267.15, "text": "although avidyā-prapaṁch is destroyed."}, {"t": 268.15, "end": 271.15, "text": "The expansion of ignorance is destroyed,"}, {"t": 271.15, "end": 275.15, "text": "but the being of self is never destroyed."}, {"t": 275.15, "end": 277.15, "text": "It is never destroyed."}, {"t": 277.15, "end": 279.15, "text": "Uthpati-damsa-virahāt."}, {"t": 279.15, "end": 283.15, "text": "Because for that self, there is no creation,"}, {"t": 283.15, "end": 286.15, "text": "there is no destruction."}, {"t": 286.15, "end": 291.15, "text": "That self is away from or above from destruction and creation."}, {"t": 291.15, "end": 294.15, "text": "Tāsmāt, nāśo, nāvāstava."}, {"t": 294.15, "end": 298.15, "text": "So, in reality, nothing is destroyed,"}, {"t": 298.15, "end": 302.15, "text": "if that being is one with this universe."}, {"t": 302.15, "end": 304.15, "text": "So nothing is destroyed."}, {"t": 304.15, "end": 307.78, "text": "This universe is also not destroyed."}, {"t": 307.78, "end": 311.78, "text": "Uthpati-damsa-virahāt."}, {"t": 311.78, "end": 317.78, "text": "It is imagined that ignorance is created"}, {"t": 317.78, "end": 322.03, "text": "and ignorance is destroyed."}, {"t": 322.03, "end": 328.03, "text": "Otherwise, ignorance itself cannot exist without that knowledge of truth."}, {"t": 328.03, "end": 335.03, "text": "So, ignorance is also not destroyable, not createable."}, {"t": 335.03, "end": 337.03, "text": "It can't be created, it can't be destroyed."}, {"t": 337.03, "end": 341.03, "text": "Because it is one with that real nature of self."}, {"t": 341.03, "end": 350.43, "text": "Yes, sovāvo nāśtamna, when it is the nature of self,"}, {"t": 350.43, "end": 353.43, "text": "that it is never destroyed."}, {"t": 353.43, "end": 356.43, "text": "How can it be destroyed at all?"}, {"t": 356.43, "end": 359.43, "text": "In creation, in protection, and in destruction."}, {"t": 359.43, "end": 363.43, "text": "This is well narrated in Spanda."}, {"t": 363.43, "end": 368.43, "text": "Avastā-yogalam-cātra-kārya-katrata-savditam."}, {"t": 368.43, "end": 373.94, "text": "These two states, which are nominated as kārya,"}, {"t": 373.94, "end": 376.94, "text": "kārya means that which is done."}, {"t": 376.94, "end": 379.94, "text": "Kārtrata means the doer."}, {"t": 379.94, "end": 386.94, "text": "The doer and done are two aspects of states."}, {"t": 386.94, "end": 391.94, "text": "Tattra, in those two states, kārya-tā-kaini."}, {"t": 391.94, "end": 394.94, "text": "The done is destroyed."}, {"t": 394.94, "end": 396.94, "text": "The aspect of done is destroyed."}, {"t": 396.94, "end": 400.94, "text": "The aspect of doer is undestroyable."}, {"t": 400.94, "end": 404.94, "text": "Kārtrataṁ punāraksha."}, {"t": 404.94, "end": 408.82, "text": "The doer is always there."}, {"t": 408.82, "end": 410.82, "text": "Kāryon-mukhā-prayat-noya."}, {"t": 410.82, "end": 412.82, "text": "Kāvalam-sotra-lupade."}, {"t": 412.82, "end": 421.82, "text": "Only that prayatna, only that force, which is to create the kārya."}, {"t": 421.82, "end": 429.82, "text": "Kārya means that which is to be created or that which is to be done."}, {"t": 429.82, "end": 433.1, "text": "Kāvalam-sotra-lupade."}, {"t": 433.1, "end": 436.1, "text": "Only that prayatna is destroyed."}, {"t": 436.1, "end": 438.1, "text": "That force is destroyed."}, {"t": 439.1, "end": 449.99, "text": "When that force is destroyed, ignorant people cry that we are also destroyed with it."}, {"t": 449.99, "end": 454.99, "text": "Kāryon-mukhā-prayatna, for instance, you have a baby."}, {"t": 454.99, "end": 456.99, "text": "That is only prayatna."}, {"t": 456.99, "end": 461.99, "text": "That is the outcome of your prayatna towards objectivity."}, {"t": 461.99, "end": 464.99, "text": "If that is destroyed, that baby is destroyed."}, {"t": 464.99, "end": 467.99, "text": "Why should you say that you are destroyed?"}, {"t": 467.99, "end": 469.99, "text": "You are never destroyed."}, {"t": 469.99, "end": 473.62, "text": "Tasmeen-luvte."}, {"t": 473.62, "end": 475.62, "text": "You look towards me."}, {"t": 475.62, "end": 477.62, "text": "Iti abhada-pritpati te."}, {"t": 477.62, "end": 486.62, "text": "Abhada-ignorant people realize in that state that we are also destroyed around with it."}, {"t": 487.62, "end": 489.62, "text": "Natyontar-mukh-bhava."}, {"t": 489.62, "end": 492.62, "text": "Sarvajat-gunas-padam-tasi-lopah."}, {"t": 492.62, "end": 493.62, "text": "Kadā-chit-syaat."}, {"t": 493.62, "end": 495.62, "text": "Anyesya-nupalambana."}, {"t": 495.62, "end": 497.62, "text": "The state of Anter-mukh-tā."}, {"t": 497.62, "end": 502.62, "text": "The state of interverted state."}, {"t": 502.62, "end": 505.62, "text": "The state what is interverted state."}, {"t": 505.62, "end": 506.62, "text": "Anter-mukh-bhava."}, {"t": 506.62, "end": 508.62, "text": "The state which is within."}, {"t": 508.62, "end": 513.74, "text": "Anyesya-nupalambana."}, {"t": 513.74, "end": 523.72, "text": "When the other agency is not present there in the absence of other agency,"}, {"t": 523.72, "end": 529.72, "text": "you can't say that that anter-mukh-bhava is destroyed."}, {"t": 529.72, "end": 537.03, "text": "Even in the state of ignorance, if you are not aware of your anter-mukh-bhava,"}, {"t": 537.03, "end": 544.37, "text": "if you are not aware of your reality of self in the state of ignorance,"}, {"t": 544.37, "end": 548.87, "text": "you can't say that it is destroyed."}, {"t": 548.87, "end": 551.87, "text": "It is there, only you are away from it."}, {"t": 551.87, "end": 557.87, "text": "You keep yourself absent from it because of your unawareness."}, {"t": 557.87, "end": 559.87, "text": "You are not aware of it."}, {"t": 559.87, "end": 560.87, "text": "That's a lopah."}, {"t": 560.87, "end": 561.87, "text": "Kadā-chit-syaat."}, {"t": 561.87, "end": 562.87, "text": "Anyesya-nupalambana."}, {"t": 562.87, "end": 567.87, "text": "If you are not realized it, how can you say that it is destroyed?"}, {"t": 567.87, "end": 569.87, "text": "It is not destroyed."}, {"t": 569.87, "end": 572.87, "text": "You have remained away from it."}, {"t": 572.87, "end": 576.87, "text": "This is explained in Spandha."}, {"t": 576.87, "end": 579.87, "text": "This is explained in Spandha."}]}